exports[`generateProject: team-platform > matches golden output for key files > CLAUDE.md 1`] = `
"# Acme

## Starting a fresh session

Run \`/start-session\` before doing anything else. It reads SESSION_LOG and NEXT_STEPS, checks git state, and prints a 5-line briefing so you know exactly where things stand.

## Project context

Acme application This is a team-team project built by a mid-size team using an Nx monorepo. The codebase follows strict module boundaries -- every app and service is independent, with shared code living in \`libs/\`. Multi-tenancy is implemented via row-level isolation. Internationalization is enabled with locales: en, ar.

## Tech stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Frontend (web) | Next.js 15 (App Router, RSC, Server Actions) |
| Frontend (admin) | Vite + React 19 (SPA) |
| Backend (api) | Go (Chi, hexagonal architecture) |
| Backend (worker) | Go (Chi, hexagonal architecture) |
| Database | PostgreSQL |
| ORM (Go) | sqlc |
| Auth | Clerk |
| API style | REST |
| Monorepo | Nx + pnpm workspaces |
| Formatting | Biome |
| CI | GitHub Actions |
| Hosting | Vercel + Fly.io |

## Where rules live

Rules auto-load by glob. Never duplicate rules -- edit the canonical file.

| File | Scope |
|------|-------|
| \`CLAUDE.md\` (this file) | Always loaded -- project-wide constitution |
| \`.claude/rules/frontend.md\` | \`apps/*/src/**/*.{ts,tsx}\` -- React / Next.js rules |
| \`.claude/rules/frontend.md\` | \`apps/*/src/**/*.{ts,tsx}\` -- React / Vite rules |
| \`.claude/rules/backend-go.md\` | \`services/**/*.go\` -- Go rules |
| \`.claude/rules/database.md\` | \`db/**/*\` -- Database & migration rules |
| \`.claude/rules/testing.md\` | \`**/*.{test,spec}.{ts,tsx,go}\` -- Testing rules |
| \`.claude/rules/design-system.md\` | \`packages/ui/**\`, \`packages/design-tokens/**\`, \`*/components/**\` -- Design system rules |

## Always-true rules

### Module boundaries
- Apps and services are **independent**. No app may import from another app.
- Shared code goes in \`libs/\`. Each lib has a barrel \`index.ts\`.
- Import from libs using workspace aliases (\`@acme/lib-name\`), never relative \`../\` paths.

### File size limits
- TypeScript / TSX: **250 lines max**. Split or extract.
- Go files: **400 lines max**. Split into focused files.
- C# files: **300 lines max**. One class per file.
- If a file exceeds the limit, refactor before adding more code.

### No god files
- No file may export more than 7 public symbols.
- No barrel file may re-export from more than 10 modules.
- No React component file may define more than 1 exported component.

### Tests
- Every new public function, endpoint, or component **must** ship with tests.
- Minimum coverage gate: 80% on new code.
- Test files live next to source: \`foo.ts\` -> \`foo.test.ts\`, \`foo.go\` -> \`foo_test.go\`.

### Security
- **Never** commit secrets, tokens, API keys, or credentials.
- Use environment variables via \`.env\` (gitignored) and \`.env.example\` (committed).
- Validate all external input at the boundary (API routes, form handlers).
- Sanitize data before rendering to prevent XSS.
- Auth is handled by Clerk. Never roll custom auth middleware.

### Commits
- Use **Conventional Commits**: \`type(scope): message\`
- Types: \`feat\`, \`fix\`, \`refactor\`, \`test\`, \`docs\`, \`chore\`, \`ci\`, \`perf\`
- Scope = app or lib name (e.g., \`feat(web): add dashboard page\`)
- Never skip pre-commit hooks (\`--no-verify\` is forbidden).

### Multi-tenancy
- Tenancy model: **row-level**
- Every DB table that holds tenant data **must** have a \`tenant_id\` column.
- Every query against tenant data **must** filter by \`tenant_id\`. No exceptions.
- Never expose data across tenant boundaries. Test with multiple tenants.

### Internationalization
- All user-facing strings go through the i18n system. Never hard-code UI text.
- Supported locales: en, ar
- Translation keys use dot notation: \`feature.component.label\`
- New features must include translations for all supported locales.

## Project lifecycle

This project follows a phased approach. Check \`PROJECT_STATUS.md\` for current phase.

| Phase | Key Skills | Gate |
|-------|-----------|------|
| **Discovery** | \`/discover\`, \`/research\` | PRD complete, MVP scoped, competitors researched |
| **Specification** | \`/spec\`, \`/plan-feature\` | Feature specs with acceptance criteria, data model, API design |
| **Architecture** | \`/adr\`, \`/plan-review\` | ADRs for key decisions, schema finalized |
| **Development** | \`/new-feature\`, \`/commit\`, \`/self-review\` | Acceptance criteria met, tests passing |
| **Review** | \`/self-review\`, \`/design-review\`, \`/sync-docs\` | All gates passed, docs in sync |
| **Deployment** | \`/deploy\`, \`/local-setup doctor\` | Staging verified, monitoring configured |

Run the \`phase-gate\` agent before transitioning between phases. It validates completeness.

**Before writing any code:**
1. Run \`/discover\` to validate the product idea and gather requirements
2. Run \`/research <competitor>\` to understand the competitive landscape
3. Run \`/spec <feature>\` for each MVP feature
4. Run \`/plan-feature <feature>\` to break specs into tasks

## Workflow rules

1. **Discover before spec.** Run \`/discover\` and \`/research\` before writing specs.
2. **Spec before code.** Run \`/spec\` and get acceptance criteria before implementing.
3. **Read before writing.** Always read a file before editing it. Understand context.
4. **Plan before coding.** For changes touching 3+ files, write a brief plan first.
5. **Small, focused changes.** One logical change per commit. No kitchen-sink PRs.
6. **Run tests before committing.** If tests fail, fix them before pushing.
7. **Update docs.** If behavior changes, run \`/sync-docs\` to keep everything in sync.
8. **Log sessions.** After meaningful work, \`/sync-docs\` updates SESSION_LOG automatically.
9. **Save learnings.** When something goes wrong or a pattern works well, save it to memory for future sessions.

## Feedback capture (critical)

The system learns from every interaction. Follow these rules **automatically** — do not wait for the developer to ask:

### When the developer corrects you
- If they say "no", "don't do that", "revert", "I don't like this" → **immediately save a feedback memory** explaining what went wrong and what they prefer instead.
- The memory must be specific: "Developer prefers X over Y because Z" — not just "changed X".
- Check existing memories before making the same type of decision again.

### When the developer doesn't like a UI/design
- Run \`/iterate <component>\` to explore alternatives with visual examples.
- Present 2-3 options before making changes. Never assume what they want.
- After they confirm, save the design preference to memory.
- If the preference is broad (applies to all similar components), update \`.claude/rules/design-system.md\`.

### When a bug is found
- Save a memory describing: what caused the bug, how it was fixed, and what pattern to avoid.
- If the bug reveals a missing rule, add the rule to the relevant \`.claude/rules/\` file.
- Write a regression test that would have caught the bug.

### When a pattern works well
- If the developer confirms something was done right (especially a non-obvious choice), save a positive feedback memory.
- Example: "Single bundled PR was the right call for this refactor — don't split small refactors unnecessarily."

## Token-efficiency rules

- Do NOT re-read files you have already read in this session unless they changed.
- Do NOT output entire file contents when making small edits. Use targeted edits.
- Do NOT explain code you just wrote unless asked. The code should be self-documenting.
- Keep responses concise. No filler phrases or unnecessary commentary.
- When searching, use targeted globs rather than recursive full-tree scans.

## Skills

| Skill | Phase | Description |
|-------|-------|-------------|
| \`/start-session\` | Any | Read SESSION_LOG + NEXT_STEPS + git state. Print 5-line briefing. |
| \`/discover\` | Discovery | Guided product discovery with competitive research. Generates PRD. |
| \`/research <topic>\` | Discovery | Deep competitive and technical research on a topic. |
| \`/spec <feature>\` | Specification | Create detailed feature spec with user stories and acceptance criteria. |
| \`/plan-feature <feature>\` | Specification | Break a spec into implementable tasks with dependencies. |
| \`/adr <decision>\` | Architecture | Create an Architecture Decision Record. |
| \`/plan-review\` | Architecture | Challenge a plan with engineering rigor. |
| \`/new-feature <name>\` | Development | Scaffold a new feature across the relevant stack(s). |
| \`/commit\` | Development | Stage, validate, and create a conventional commit. |
| \`/self-review\` | Review | Run comprehensive self-review on current changes. |
| \`/iterate <component>\` | Development | Iterate on UI based on feedback — shows alternatives, saves preferences. |
| \`/sync-docs\` | Any | Comprehensive document sync — detects drift, updates all docs. |
| \`/local-setup\` | Any | Bootstrap, doctor, or reset the local dev environment. |
| \`/deploy\` | Deployment | Trigger a release workflow. |
| \`/design-review\` | Review UI changes against the design system quality bar. |
| \`/figma-sync\` | Sync components/tokens between code and Figma. |
| \`/figma-implement\` | Implement a Figma design as production code. |

## Sub-agents

| Agent | Model | Use for |
|-------|-------|---------|
| \`product-analyst\` | opus | Identifies requirement gaps, edge cases, missing business logic |
| \`phase-gate\` | sonnet | Validates phase completeness before transitions |
| \`architect\` | opus | Designing features, making architectural decisions |
| \`code-reviewer\` | opus | Reviewing PRs and code changes |
| \`security-auditor\` | sonnet | OWASP checks, auth flow analysis, secrets scanning |
| \`test-writer\` | sonnet | Generating tests for existing or new code |
| \`performance-analyst\` | sonnet | N+1 detection, bundle analysis, API profiling |
| \`refactoring-specialist\` | sonnet | Systematic refactors with test gates |
| \`react-architect\` | sonnet | React component design, RSC patterns, hooks |
| \`react-architect\` | sonnet | React component design, state management, hooks |
| \`go-expert\` | sonnet | Go concurrency, error handling, performance |
| \`design-reviewer\` | sonnet | Design system compliance, accessibility, token usage, visual consistency |

## Forbidden actions

- **NEVER** run \`git push --force\` to \`main\` or \`master\`.
- **NEVER** run \`rm -rf /\`, \`rm -rf ~\`, or \`rm -rf .\` outside of \`node_modules\`/\`dist\`.
- **NEVER** modify \`.env\` files directly. Only modify \`.env.example\`.
- **NEVER** disable TypeScript strict mode or ESLint/Biome rules.
- **NEVER** commit \`node_modules\`, \`dist\`, \`.next\`, or build artifacts.
- **NEVER** use \`any\` in TypeScript. Use \`unknown\` and narrow.
- **NEVER** skip the pre-commit hook with \`--no-verify\`.
- **NEVER** write to files outside the project root.
- **NEVER** install packages globally. Use project-local dependencies.
- **NEVER** store secrets in code, config files, or commit history.
- **NEVER** hardcode colors (hex/rgb/hsl). Use design tokens from \`@acme/design-tokens\`.
- **NEVER** use inline \`style={{}}\` on React components. Use Tailwind + tokens.
- **NEVER** skip accessibility — keyboard nav, focus states, contrast ratios are mandatory.
"
`;

